§ `VerifyUnsatRequirementFixture`

-- A rule split at its seam (a top-level IMPLIES) whose requirement cannot
-- hold at all. The requirement is unsatisfiable, and so nothing within scope
-- meets it. Both are said, once each: `unreachable-outcome` at the rule and
-- `unsat` at the requirement. The walk over the rule as written reaches the
-- requirement too, and must not say `unsat` a second time.
GIVEN s IS A BOOLEAN
      x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a requirement nobody can meet` IS
  s IMPLIES (x AND (NOT x))
